  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Readable
  Title: Exhibit I - The Morvayne Coffin
  Body: 'Oak, iron and lead. c. 1640.


    Recovered from the family crypt beneath
    this house, where it had lain sealed for two centuries.


    Visitors often
    ask why the lock is fitted to the inside of the lid. The museum has no explanation
    to offer.'
  ReadClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: d827ef23d1b788f4b92b1131a21aa803, type: 3}
  Verb: Read
